  "body": "`crates/app/tests/scripting.rs` (the job-script suite) crashed with SIGSEGV once during a quick gate on macOS (M-series):\n\n```\nprocess didn't exit successfully: `.../deps/scripting-32873f0c2458da46 --test-threads=6` (signal: 11, SIGSEGV: invalid memory reference)\n```\n\n- Tree: `issue/370-tool-csys-align` at upstream/main `a6e9c7c`, plus a STEP-reader-only change that touches nothing in `script/`. The crash is not caused by that branch.\n- It happened during `scripts/gate.sh quick` (`cargo test -p camcraft-app`), while a second worktree's gate was building and testing at the same time, so the machine was under heavy load.\n- The same binary, rerun alone 45 times with `--test-threads=6`, passed every time. The crash is intermittent and load-dependent.\n\nA segfault in a test binary means memory unsafety somewhere on the scripting path: the script engine, the FFI, or a flecs world shared across test threads. Per the Prime Directive, it must be found, not retried away.\n\n**Done means:** the cause is found (try `--test-threads=1` vs many under `stress`, and an ASan or `RUST_BACKTRACE` + lldb run) and fixed, with a stress test or note that pins it.\n",
